# LLM API Configuration
# Copy this file to .env and add your API keys
# The system will auto-detect which provider is available
# Priority order: Azure OpenAI → OpenAI → Gemini → Anthropic → Groq → Ollama

# Tesseract OCR Path (if not in system PATH)
# Windows: TESSERACT_CMD=C:\Users\suraj.yadav\AppData\Local\Programs\Tesseract-OCR\tesseract.exe
# macOS/Linux: Usually auto-detected if installed via package manager

# Option 1: Azure OpenAI
# AZURE_OPENAI_KEY=your-azure-key-here
# AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=https://your-resource.openai.azure.com/
# AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT=gpt-4o
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_VERSION=2024-02-15-preview

# Option 2: OpenAI (standard API)
# OPENAI_API_KEY=your-openai-key-here
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o

# Option 3: Google Gemini
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=your-google-api-key-here
# GOOGLE_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash-exp

# Option 4: Anthropic Claude
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-anthropic-key-here
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-20250514

# Option 5: Groq (fast inference)
# GROQ_API_KEY=your-groq-key-here
# GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.2-90b-vision-preview

# Option 6: Ollama (local/self-hosted)
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
# OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2-vision

# Usage:
# 1. Copy this file: cp .env.example .env
# 2. Uncomment and fill in ONE of the provider sections above
# 3. Install Tesseract OCR (see README.md)
# 4. Run: python src/pipeline.py --input "data/raw/Group A/M047FJFL.001"
